# Reference listing pages, GENERATED by docs/make.jl from the public surface —
# never hand-edited, a pure function of the source, rebuilt by every docs build.
# The 95-reference.md landing page is hand-written and IS tracked.
#
# docs/src/60-benchmarks.md is deliberately NOT ignored: it is a measurement,
# not a derivation. It cannot be reproduced from the source alone, it names the
# commit and machine it describes, and it is the evidence the status page and
# README point at. A docs build regenerates it, so `git status` shows it dirty
# after any build that ran the suite — commit it only when you meant to record
# a new measurement, from a clean tree.
docs/src/95-reference/
